 <self>`. Mutually exclusive with `--author`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```\nentire dispatch --me\nentire dispatch --repos owner/repo --me\nentire dispatch --repos owner/repo --author teammate@company.com --since 14d\nentire dispatch --local --all-branches --me\n```\n\n### Identity resolution for `--me`\n\n`--me` resolves at flag-parse time to a single email value, with mode-dependent fallback:\n\n- **Cloud mode (`--repos ...` or default):** server-side resolution. Send `me: true` in the request body — the server uses the bearer token's `user_id` (see `api/auth_tokens.go:14`). No client-side email lookup needed; this also gracefully handles the \"I don't know my own Entire-account email\" case.\n- **Local mode (`--local`):** client-side resolution. Read `git config user.email` from the active repo. Fail with a clear error if unset (`run 'git config user.email' first, or pass --author <email>`).\n\n`--author <email>` is uniform: in cloud mode it goes in the request body as `author`; in local mode it filters commits by exact author-email match.\n\n### Cloud plumbing\n\nMirror the existing `--voice` flag's path:\n\n1. **Flag → Options.** Extend `Options` in `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go` with two fields: `Me bool` and `Author string`. Update `ResolveOptions` to accept them, validate mutual exclusion (`--me` + `--author` is an error), and reject `--me` when `git config user.email` is unset *and* mode is local. (For cloud mode, `--me` does not need an email locally — the server resolves it.)\n2. **Options → request body.** Extend `CreateDispatchRequest` in `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud.go` (line 58) with two new omitempty fields:\n   ```go\n   Author string `json:\"author,omitempty\"`\n   Me     bool   `json:\"me,omitempty\"`\n   ```\n   Wire them through in `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go` where the request is constructed.\n3. **Server change (prerequisite, NOT in this repo).** The `/api/v1/dispatches/generate` endpoint must learn to filter by either `author` (string match against the checkpoint's author identity) or `me` (filter by the bearer token's `user_id`). Without this server change, the flags will be silently ignored. **This must be coordinated as a separate server PR landing first.** The CLI change should still ship with the flags marked clearly as \"requires server side support\" until the server PR is deployed everywhere.\n\n### Local plumbing\n\nLocal mode reads from `entire/checkpoints/v1` on disk (`cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go`). The filter is applied client-side after checkpoint discovery:\n\n1. **Resolve target email.** Compute `targetEmail` once: from `--author` if set, else from `git config user.email` if `--me`. Empty string means \"no filter.\"\n2. **Filter checkpoints by author.** Each checkpoint on `entire/checkpoints/v1` has a git author signature. After enumerating checkpoints in the time window, filter to those whose author email matches `targetEmail` (case-insensitive). Reuse the existing checkpoint enumeration in `mode_local.go` — no new git plumbing — and add a single filter step before the bullets are built.\n3. **Empty-result UX.** If the filter removes all checkpoints, render a friendly \"no checkpoints in window for <email>\" message rather than an empty dispatch.\n\n### Wizard\n\nThe interactive flow (`cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go`) currently asks for mode, time window, repos/branches, and voice. Add one new step: **scope** (huh select):\n\n- \"Just me\" → sets `--me`\n- \"Specific person…\" → free-text input bound to `--author`\n- \"Everyone\" → no filter (default)\n\nThis step appears after repo/branch selection and before the voice prompt. Skipped in flag-driven mode (see `shouldRunDispatchWizard` at `dispatch.go:115`).\n\n### Files to modify\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go` — flag definitions, plumbing into `parseDispatchFlags`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go` — `Options` fields, `ResolveOptions` signature + validation.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud.go` — `CreateDispatchRequest` fields.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go` — populate request fields from `Options`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go` — apply author filter to enumerated checkpoints; emit empty-result message.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go` — new \"scope\" step.\n- (Optional, helpful) Update README / `--help` long description in `dispatch.go:36–42` with the new examples.\n\n### Tests\n\nMirror the existing patterns:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options_test.go` — cover: `--me` and `--author` plumb correctly; mutual exclusion errors; `--me` without `git config user.email` errors *only* in local mode; trimming/normalizing of email.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud_test.go` — verify `author` and `me` fields appear in the POST body (and are omitted when unset).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local_test.go` — fixture with two checkpoints from different authors; assert the filter keeps only the matching ones; case-insensitive match; empty-result path renders the friendly message. Use `testutil.InitRepo` + `testutil.GitCommit` to control author identity (the test pattern at `mode_local_test.go:549`/`576` already sets `GIT_AUTHOR_*`).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard_test.go` — drive the new scope step, assert flag values produced.\n- All new tests use `t.Parallel()` per the repo convention.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Lint + tests:** `mise run check` (fmt + lint + unit + integration + canary).\n2. **Local-mode end-to-end (no API cost):** in a scratch repo with two checkpoints authored by different emails, run:\n   - `entire dispatch --local --me` → only your checkpoints\n   - `entire dispatch --local --author other@example.com` → only theirs\n   - `entire dispatch --local` → both, unchanged from today\n3. **Cloud-mode dry run before server is ready:** confirm via `cloud_test.go` that the new fields are in the JSON body. Once the server-side filter ships, run:\n   - `entire dispatch --repos entireio/cli --me --since 14d`\n   - `entire dispatch --repos entireio/cli --author <teammate-email> --since 14d`\n4. **Wizard:** run `entire dispatch` with no args; tab through to the new scope step; verify it produces the expected flag values (visible in dispatch output / via debug logging).\n5. **Accessibility mode:** `ACCESSIBLE=1 entire dispatch` — confirm the new wizard step uses `NewAccessibleForm` (per `CLAUDE.md` accessibility guidelines).\n\n## Out of scope (future)\n\n- Multiple `--author` values (filter by a small group). Easy follow-up: change `Author` to `[]string` once the server supports it.\n- A `--not-me` flag (everyone except me).\n- Storing the Entire-account email locally so `--me` could resolve client-side without depending on the bearer token. Worth doing if other commands grow `--me`-style flags, but unnecessary for this one.\n- Folding `entire recap`'s \"you\" view into dispatch — different purpose (dashboard vs narrative), keep them separate.\n\n## Server-side dependency (call-out)\n\n**Cloud-mode filtering requires a server change** to `/api/v1/dispatches/generate`. The CLI portion of this plan can ship first behind a clearly-documented \"requires backend support deployed\" caveat in `--help`, OR coordinate with the server PR so they land together. Recommend coordinating both PRs to land in the same release window.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"880e25a5-d8f3-456a-ba86-e6292592b639","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dvydra/src/entireio/cli","sessionId":"f3ed46f4-4f7a-4a0e-a4ad-d1ffab226392","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"main","slug":"yes-design-this-for-snoopy-pond"}
