{"parentUuid":"4fa7f88f-92d8-4906-beef-68e7c0dd6dd3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BYEup8iERrburcTS1CuBRV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Walking through the path your `--me` / `--author <email>` takes in local mode.\n\n**1. Flag parsing** (`cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:71-78`) — cobra reads `--author` and `--me`, then `parseDispatchFlags` calls `ResolveOptions` (`cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go:12`), which trims `flagAuthor`, rejects `--author + --me` together, and stores both on `Options.Author` / `Options.Me`. No git lookup yet — `--me` is just a marker at this point.\n\n**2. Identity resolution** — when `Run()` dispatches to `runLocal()` (`cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:29`), the very first thing after parsing the time window is `resolveLocalAuthorFilter` (`mode_local.go:374`):\n```\nopts.Author != \"\"   → return strings.ToLower(opts.Author)\nopts.Me           → shell out to `git -C <firstRepo> config user.email`\n                     return strings.ToLower(email), or error if unset\notherwise           → return \"\" (no filter)\n```\nThe result is the lowercased target email — one string for the whole run.\n\n**3. Per-repo enumeration** (`mode_local.go:55-71`) — a `errgroup` walks each repo in `repoRoots` concurrently. For each repo, `enumerateRepoCandidates` returns a `[]candidate` (one per checkpoint in the window, branch-filtered, with the checkpoint ID and other metadata). This is the unchanged path.\n\n**4. Author filter step** (`mode_local.go:62-67`) — if `authorFilter != \"\"`, `filterCandidatesByAuthor` runs on the candidate list. It:\n   - Shells out to `git log entire/checkpoints/v1 --format=%ae%x00%s%x00%x00` once per repo (`loadCommitAuthorsByCheckpoint`, `mode_local.go:432`).\n   - Parses each record into `(authorEmail, \"Checkpoint: <id>\")`. Builds a `map[checkpointID]authorEmail`.\n   - Iterates the candidates: keeps only those whose ID is in the map *and* whose recorded author (lowercased) matches the target.\n   - Candidates whose ID isn't on `entire/checkpoints/v1` (shouldn't happen in normal flow, but can in tests that bypass the metadata write) are dropped — defensive.\n\n**5. Empty-result short circuit** (`mode_local.go:75-77`) — after all per-repo goroutines finish, if the filter was active and zero candidates remain, return `no checkpoints in window for author \"<email>\"` instead of going through the LLM and getting an empty-markdown error.\n\n**6. Why `entire/checkpoints/v1` is the source of truth** — every checkpoint has a metadata commit there, authored at `WriteCommitted` time using `git config user.name/user.email` of whoever created the checkpoint (`strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:196`, `cpkg.GetGitAuthorFromRepo`). So:\n   - Checkpoints *you* created on this machine → authored by your local git user.\n   - Checkpoints fetched from a teammate's push → authored by their git user.\n   - `--me` filters to the first; `--author teammate@x` filters to the second.\n\nEnd-to-end: `dispatch.go → ResolveOptions → runLocal → resolveLocalAuthorFilter → enumerateRepoCandidates → filterCandidatesByAuthor → empty-check → generate`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_read_input_tokens":241762,"output_tokens":1264,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":241762,"cache_creation_input_tokens":679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":679},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CakUZ3kunkPkeLe2hXBE9","type":"assistant","uuid":"07e9ee57-52ae-4f43-9db0-8c934dc677ce","timestamp":"2026-05-06T01:50:19.440Z","userType":"external","entrypoint